+### Aggregate resource contract (proposed GH623 amendment)
+
+This section defines the target contract. It is not a claim of current implementation.
+The existing GH623 specification owns capacity and local-refusal approval.
+
+- One authoritative ledger bounds each role generation's retained outbound bytes
+  and operation records before the first framework retention, including encoding,
+  readiness waits, message posting, Worker-local output and serialized writes.
+- Admission counts backing storage and temporary copy overlap. Zero-length work
+  still consumes a record. Failed admission creates no pending transport waiter.
+- Accepted frames keep the existing single FIFO. Capacity exhaustion never silently
+  drops accepted EVENTs or automatically retries unanswered CALLs.
+- Caller settlement does not release another owner's payload, pending correlation,
+  handler or tombstone. Release follows actual retirement, exactly once.
+- Worker-owned credit release cannot depend on a callback to a parked main thread.
+  Permanent tombstone saturation has a bounded terminal path without a new call.
+- Handler invocation reserves both concurrency and maximum answer storage before
+  application effects. Control and answer reserves cannot admit ordinary data.
+- Host UI commands remain charged through forwarding until physical consumption.
+  Native facts have a separate bound before filtering. A local queue bound cannot
+  be presented as a bound on the full pipeline.
+- Absolute queue, write, call, retirement and close budgets are distinct. A successful
+  short write or renewed polling timeout cannot renew the operation's original clock.
+- Schema owners bound decoded elements and storage before allocation. Receive capacity
+  must fit the largest supported encoded response, including its envelope.
+- A generation's late callback cannot release successor credit. Physical cleanup is
+  observed separately from a terminal state or termination request.
+- Fixed buffers, decoded objects, application retention, runtime and OS memory remain
+  separate terms. Logical transport accounting alone does not establish total RSS.
